# No env vars are used by this app. Credentials (access token, client ID/secret,
# Anthropic key) and the MCP endpoint are supplied per-request from the UI —
# this app is publicly shared, so a server-side default would be usable by
# every visitor.
#
# This file is a placeholder for forks. Nothing in src/ reads process.env, so
# adding variables here has no effect on its own: to make a fork read them, wire
# them into the resolver functions in src/lib/config.ts (resolveAccessToken,
# resolveClientId, resolveClientSecret, resolveLoginUrl, resolveAnthropicKey),
# each of which currently returns only what the caller passed in.
#
# Only do that for a deployment you control. A server-side credential is used
# implicitly by every visitor, which is the reason it was removed here.
